# Line endings and binary classification.
#
# Why this file exists: without it, how every text file in this repo is stored
# and checked out depends on each machine's `core.autocrlf`, which is a local
# setting nothing in the repo controls. Two checkouts with different values
# produce whole-file diffs against each other for reasons that have nothing to
# do with the content.
#
# `text=auto` normalises to LF in the object store for everything not matched
# below. Unity 6.6 writes LF for scenes, ScriptableObjects, prefabs and .meta
# (importer, ContentBuilder and SceneBuilder output alike), so the Unity YAML
# rules below check out LF too. A platform-default (CRLF) checkout would be
# rewritten to LF by Unity on the next import and dirty the tree forever.
#
# The huge scene diffs are not line endings. A full SceneBuilder regeneration
# reassigns every fileID, which rewrites most lines of the YAML. See
# CLAUDE.md, "scenes are generated".
* text=auto

# Shell scripts need LF: a CRLF checkout makes the shebang read as
# `/bin/sh` and the script dies with "bad interpreter".
tools/githooks/* text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf

# Unity YAML: LF in the working tree, matching what Unity writes.
*.unity   text eol=lf
*.prefab  text eol=lf
*.asset   text eol=lf
*.meta    text eol=lf
*.mat     text eol=lf
*.anim    text eol=lf
*.controller text eol=lf

# Binaries: never diffed, never converted. Git guesses right on these today;
# saying so removes the guess.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.psd  binary
*.tga  binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.wav  binary
*.mp3  binary
*.ogg  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.fbx  binary
*.dll  binary
*.pdb  binary
*.unitypackage binary
